WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.370
Do you have a moment?

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.190
Yamaguchi-sensei.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:09.350
Right. This is all new to me,
so I sort of forgot about this.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.170
I got this a while ago, but I overlooked it.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.610
It looks like we were
entered for something called

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:18.330
<b>Kanagawa Prefecture Middle School Spring Season Preliminaries (Nippon Junior High School Physical Culture Association)</b>

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:18.330
<b>Prefecture East District Bracket</b>

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:18.330
<b>Final</b>

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.490
the Kanagawa Prefecture Middle
School Spring Season Preliminaries.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.490
<b>F
u
u
r
i
n

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.490
<b>B
a
s
e
b
a
l
l

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>on Preliminaries (Nippon Junior High School Physical Culture Association)</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>Kanagawa</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>Prefecture</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>Middle</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>School Spring Seas</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>East District</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>Prefecture</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>Bracket</b>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
<b>Final</b>

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.920
We've seriously got a tourney in two weeks?

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:01.050
<b>What's With This Guy?!</b>

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.170
Oh, right. I guess the first-years wouldn't know.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.390
The Japanese National 
Youth Baseball Tournament.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.970
Also known as the rubber-ball nationals.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.440
I didn't think we'd signed up for it
this year, so this is a real surprise.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:15.230
We only just scraped together nine players.
We haven't even had a practice game yet.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.600
It's way too early to play in any tournaments.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.530
And in just two weeks?

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.700
Hm, true. We haven't really
practiced as a team yet.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.490
With only nine of us,
if one person gets sick, we're out.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.030
So should we back out?

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.250
No, let's go for it.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.460
This is an opportunity.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.340
If we do go, are Nishina-kun and
Sakura-senpai our only pitchers?

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.040
Nishina ain't no good.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:35.920
He's useless.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.210
What are you going to do?

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.840
I don't mind if you choose not to participate.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.060
<i>That way, this tournament
won't ruin my precious weekend.</i>

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.770
No, of course we'll play in it.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.010
We wanted to play some
practice games, anyway.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:56.390
We won't set ourselves
a goal on where we place,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.160
but tournament experience
will be invaluable.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.490
I s-see.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.330
For now, we'll determine 
how strong we really are.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.540
Back home!

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.860
Dammit.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.780
Why am I the only one who 
has to do stamina training?

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:39.680
Last one.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.150
Down the pipe.

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:46.860
Nice ball!

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.500
See you later.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.750
Good session today. Bye!

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.300
Hey, first-years!

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.390
One of you come help me
with the field covers.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.510
Coming!

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:07.910
I'll go.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.460
Put this away for me.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:11.780
Why do I have to do your part, too—

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.190
You're ignoring me?!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.410
So heavy...

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.960
Oh, Anita.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.170
Grab that end.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.230
Senpai, if we're gonna go to this tournament,

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.820
oughtn't we do somethin'
'bout the pitcher situation?

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:27.980
Huh?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.360
Nishina ain't gonna be any use to us,

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.340
and there ain't no tellin' how many
runs Sakura-senpai's gonna give up.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:41.300
She's got good control, and when it comes to
breaking balls, she's got sinkers and sliders.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.940
I get why Nishina and the others got
done over, but with just those two,

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.200
we'll never be the best in the region.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.680
Best in the region?

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.230
As if. We're not aiming <i>that</i> high.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.700
Come on, grab that end.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.020
But if we win two games, 
we're in the semi-finals.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:06.960
And if we make the semi-finals,
we play two games on the third day.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.290
What's she going on about now?

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.160
Well... I have a hunch.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:17.340
No matter how you look at it,
we ain't gettin' nowhere with one pitcher.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:21.460
And sweet, delicate Sakura-senpai will only
be at her best for one or two games, tops.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.850
The obvious answer is
to find at least one more pitcher.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:31.100
As captain, you need to
think about these things.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.310
What's the point of enterin'
a tourney and <i>not</i> tryna win it?!

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.770
No, it'll be fine.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.480
I appreciate your enthusiasm.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.950
With you guys on board,
we'll put up a decent fight, for sure.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:51.910
But it isn't yet time for us
to be overreaching ourselves.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:56.810
All right, Nishina, Chisato, 
help us roll out the sheet.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:57.540
Okay.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.620
Sure.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.200
Nishina, pull that over there.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.190
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.630
I'll take this side.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.350
Okay.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.350
I'm leaving now.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:08.100
Please make sure you lock up.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.270
Okay.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.790
This team ain't gonna get nowhere!

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.590
I knew Baby Boy oughtn't
be allowed near the captaincy.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:16.980
"Baby Boy"?

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:21.650
He don't care one bit 'bout
winnin' this tournament!

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:26.600
And without a coach,
we need a <i>real</i> captain to take charge!

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.280
Instead, we got this loosey-goosey fella
who ain't fit to lead anythin'!

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.620
You think?

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:36.750
I think he's nice. But it's more than that.
He always helps everyone with their drills.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.720
He's acting like a "real" captain, if you ask me.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:40.700
Chisato!

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.560
You should pitch!

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.050
You pitched for Little, 
so I know you can do it.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:47.640
What?

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:55.000
I'm exhausted!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.270
Good morning!

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.430
Oh, morning.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.500
What's got into you, Mutsuko?

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.380
Don't you usually take the bus?

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.900
Huh? Oh, well, you know...

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:11.430
I-I thought I'd try to copy
what you do for training.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.870
I need to get in shape for the tournament.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:17.030
I see.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.980
Wh-What?

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.640
So how are things with Anita?

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.100
Think you'll get along?

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.970
Yeah. No problems so far.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:33.280
She's a really good catcher,
and she praises my good pitches.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.260
And it's easy to pitch
to someone her size.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.560
I guess I'm too small for 
anyone to see the target.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.270
Oh, no, I didn't mean it like that!

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.180
Huh?

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.690
Someone got here even earlier
than us, and they're pitching.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:48.810
It's not Nishina, is it?

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.280
Nice ball!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.110
That was amazing, Chisato.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:00.560
You're really good.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:01.660
Oh, not really...

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:06.130
<i>Wait, her pitches are way faster than mine!</i>

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.090
Fast, ain't they?

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:12.330
She was a middle reliever for Yokohama Little.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:17.400
Bet you wanna reconsider your
pitchin' lineup now, don'tcha, Captain?

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.780
Nope, not really.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:24.250
Sorry, but I don't intend to put a first-year
on the mound in an official tournament.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:28.380
Besides, I'm the captain of this team, not you.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:35.760
I can't entrust the catcher position to
someone who refuses to follow my directions.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:43.190
This formula is very important, 
so please commit it to memory.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.010
This will be on the test.

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:50.380
I can't entrust the catcher position to
someone who refuses to follow my directions.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.930
Chisato, do you want to pitch?

00:08:54.930 --> 00:09:00.430
Oh, uh, no. I just figured I'd warm up
my arm because we seem light on pitchers.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:01.560
I see.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.730
Then, let's revisit this
after the tournament.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:09.280
Right now, I need you to focus on your 
linchpin position as the center fielder.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.930
O-Okay!

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:14.990
Anita, you should be concentrating on
building up your battery with Mutsuko.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:19.650
If you go behind my back again, you'll be
switching places with me in the outfield.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:20.650
You got that?

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:24.250
<i>Who's that runt think he is?!</i>

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:29.460
<i>I was doin' him a favor. Where's he get off,
throwin' it back in my face like that?</i>

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.420
Okay, Anita, you can be our starting catcher.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:37.420
<i>Why's a wussy captain who
gave up his position to a first-year,</i>

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.670
<i>suddenly actin' like a coach?!</i>

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.390
<i>I ain't acceptin' any of this!</i>

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:43.810
Huh?

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:47.060
You want to know why Daigo's our captain?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.810
Yeah. From day one,
it ain't made a lick of sense to me.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.610
I mean, Tanba-san's a third-year.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:57.120
Or if you did it on skill,
you two have him beat, hands down.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:01.410
So I wanna know why the heck that
shrimpy Shigeno-senpai's our captain!

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.640
Because our old coach 
gave him the captaincy.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.930
Huh? That's the <i>only </i>reason?

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:09.480
We were never interested in it, anyway.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:12.410
You're basically just
a manager by another name.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.380
If anything, we're lucky Daigo wanted to do it.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:19.720
So y'all are totally fine
with him bein' captain?

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:26.070
With no coach around, he seems pleased
as punch to be tellin' the team what to do,

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:30.300
but I'll level with you: I don't wanna
listen to a fella who's worse'n me.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:34.020
An' I can't <i>stand</i> that he don't
care 'bout winnin' this tourney!

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.740
What's the big rush, Anita?

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:44.160
I mean, I know you hate losing,
but there'll be plenty of other tournaments.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:46.840
What's got you so riled up?

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:52.380
We'll see after this tournament
how good our captain is.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.570
If we get a bad result,
we can all rethink it.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:59.090
Oh... I see how it is.

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:00.910
Fine, then.

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:05.930
What's up with her?

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:09.140
She's even more intense now
than when we were in Little.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.370
There's something off about her.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:14.140
The other day, she lied
when she introduced herself.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:15.270
Huh? She lied?

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:22.740
She said she was Yokohama Little's catcher
when they got to the quarters of Nationals.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.770
I looked into it, and that's not quite true.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:26.900
What?!

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.830
It's so disappointin'.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.670
The older players are too
laid back and can't be relied on!

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:38.350
Why don't you just let it go?

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.850
In the upcoming tournament,
let's just focus on our own game.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.290
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:47.060
I'll just hafta prop up the
team by makin' all the plays

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.530
and become the captain in all but name.

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:50.710
Anita!

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:53.060
Senpai!

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.650
<i>Aw, hell. Did he just hear all that?</i>

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:59.410
Sorry about this, but I need you
to come somewhere with me.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.250
Chisato, you can go to practice.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.100
Oh, and Anita, please change into a tracksuit.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.490
We can't go to this place
wearing our school or team uniforms.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:20.420
Are they gonna make me 
drag around tires again?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.390
What are those two weirdos up to?

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:26.860
Captain?

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.650
Oh, hey, Nishina.

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:30.740
Where are you going?

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:31.970
Playing hooky?

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.310
Yeah, right.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:36.470
Hey, whaddaya say to letting
me practice pitching today?

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:37.270
Not happening.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:41.990
From now to the tournament, you need
to focus on getting your core fitness up.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.060
B-But hold on a minute!

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.420
End of discussion.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.750
We're in a hurry.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.150
Let's go, Anita.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:49.160
H-Hey!

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:53.330
Damn!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.250
I've had it!

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.500
I'm going home.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.290
I don't care.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.690
The field isn't that way.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.370
I w-was about to—

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:05.510
Let's give it our all again today!

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.310
Hey! Let go!

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.970
Excuse me!

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:11.520
Oh, you're alone?

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.480
Anita's not with you?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:17.050
Shigeno-senpai whisked her away on a date!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.980
Just kidding.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:21.610
That was a joke?!

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:25.140
We have no data on the first team we're facing,

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:27.090
so they went to do some recon.

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:31.580
He said, as she's our catcher,
she should probably tag along.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.340
Huh. He's going that far?

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:38.090
I thought he said he didn't really 
care about this tournament.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.540
I think you might have misunderstood him.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:44.830
He said we shouldn't overreach ourselves,

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.510
but he never said we're
going out there to lose.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.180
He doesn't really show it,

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:54.310
but I'm pretty sure he hates 
losing more than anyone else.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.310
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.310
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.310
Itsuki Public Middle School

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.310
We're here.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.730
Ah, there they are.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:04.160
What a stroke of luck!

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.190
They're playing a scrimmage game.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.240
Let's watch from here.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.460
Why from all the way back here?

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:17.780
An' the trees are in the way.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:20.000
We could just go stand behind the back net.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:24.690
Even out here, we don't want
to get caught spying on them.

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:25.960
It'd mean a reprimand.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.070
Why do you think I asked you 
to put on a generic tracksuit?

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:34.180
Here, use these to get a better look.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.890
Uh... But...

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.760
Don't worry.

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:39.360
I've got another pair.

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:43.190
Looks like it's an intra-team game.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.570
The ones with uniforms must be starters.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.470
<i>What's the deal with this captain?</i>

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.550
<i>I thought he didn't care 'bout winnin',</i>

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:00.000
<i>but here he is, diligently scoutin'
out our first-round opponents!</i>

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.410
<i>I don't get it!</i>

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.650
<i>The heck's goin' on?</i>

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:03.960
Look, Anita.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.880
That's Itsuki Middle's ace.

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:13.680
Well, probably.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:16.160
No, that's their ace, 100 percent.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:21.480
So what should we do after school?

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.330
Wanna go to the batting cages again?

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:29.030
Nah. Going there every day
puts a dent in the wallet.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:34.450
They should have Senior League practice
on weekdays too, not just on weekends.

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:37.350
That's where I get jealous of Nishina.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.450
He's got practice every day.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.560
And he's a starter already, too.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.710
Hey, Nishina.

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:46.820
On your all-girl team,
you're gonna be their ace for sure, right?

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:48.290
Of course I am!

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.560
I knew it.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:54.530
But just you wait. We'll be starters
in the Senior League, too!

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.700
Let's aim for Nationals like 
when we played for the Lions.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.030
Yeah!

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:09.950
<i>Those guys are definitely gonna
take a step up in the Senior League.</i>

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:14.480
<i>Should I really let myself 
rot away in this team?</i>

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.640
<i>The school year only just started.
Maybe I should forget the scholarship,</i>

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:22.910
<i>enter a public school,
and play in the Senior League as well?</i>

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:30.140
Wow, a pitching machine!

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:32.090
Didn't know we had one of these.

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:36.500
Well, this <i>is</i> a private school,
and the team was strong in the past.

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:38.260
If the machine's out,

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.050
does that mean Itsuki's
pitcher is pretty fast?

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:42.100
Yes.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.560
Based on what me and Anita saw,

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:48.730
we reckon he pitches
around the 120 kmph mark.

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:51.220
120 kmph?!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.810
He doesn't use breaking balls, 
so far as we could tell,

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:56.950
but if we can't hit those fastballs,
we won't get anywhere.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.820
So we're focusing on batting.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:01.040
Bingo.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:04.620
Everyone! Let's do our best
so we can hit those fastballs!

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:06.080
All right!

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:18.890
Next up, Nishina!

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:22.290
<i>What should I do about this tournament?</i>

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:24.540
<i>They'll struggle without me.</i>

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.190
<i>Oh well. Not my problem.</i>

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:36.240
Okay, here we go!

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.450
Please!

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:41.990
He glanced it!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:44.160
He's got a good swing.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:49.280
Wow! He's really hitting them back.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.630
Nobody practices batting more than him.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:55.340
<i>I didn't get near those balls,
and he's just casually...</i>

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.750
<i>If I quit now,</i>

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:01.410
<i>it'll look like I ran away because
I couldn't keep up with him.</i>

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:04.770
<i>I can't do that!</i>

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:09.230
<i>First, I'll show him up and then quit!</i>

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:14.950
Who's that?

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:17.070
They're not wearing our school's uniform.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.130
Hey, you over there!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.790
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.790
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.790
Itsuki Public Middle School

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:25.790
What? Six of their players are girls?

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:26.860
Yes.

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:30.430
And it seems like they only 
have nine players total.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:32.250
Barely enough to field a team.

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:33.800
I see.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:38.460
I didn't get to see the pitcher today, 
but I'll try to sneak back another time.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:39.420
All right.

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:42.220
Please copy today's video
onto the computer.

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:51.400
Senpai.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:53.000
Yes?

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:56.110
I'm gonna be honest,
I don't get your thinkin' at all.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:57.530
Huh?

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:00.370
If you care enough 'bout
winnin' to scout the other team,

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:02.850
why don'tcha prep another pitcher?

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:08.130
I know it'd be sudden, 
but Chisato's got experience.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:11.290
Ain't no harm in lettin'
her practice pitchin' a bit.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.250
It'd take some of the pressure
off Sakura-senpai, too.

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:20.690
And why <i>can't</i> Nishina get up on the
mound, just 'cause he's a first-year?

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:25.260
You oughta test him and let him
explore his limits without goin' past 'em.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:30.510
It looks like you still don't 
understand your position.

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:31.190
Huh?

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:33.900
You're also being tested right now.

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:39.250
Instead of worrying about
all our pitching options,

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:43.320
you should be thinking about how
to win the first game with just Mutsuko.

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:47.850
That's why I brought you scouting
with me. Do you understand?

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:52.440
I'll spell it out for you.
I think Mutsuko can do it.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:58.270
If they end up hitting her pitches, 
that's on you as the catcher.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.450
<i>I ain't ever givin' him
the chance to blame me.</i>

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:05.140
<i>With me callin' the shots,
we're gonna shut 'em out.</i>

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.600
Nice ball!

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:23.490
On the next one,
aim low to the inside.

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:30.080
Good work!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.100
Yeah, good work!

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:34.300
Everyone's really improved.

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:35.330
Yeah.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:38.260
Our opponents are scarier than I thought,

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:41.380
but with our potential, 
winning isn't out of the question.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:42.610
Yeah.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:46.340
I'm ready to get up on the mound the day
after tomorrow and pitch with all I've got.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:48.300
We're counting on you.

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.180
Hey, how long are you
going to hog that spot?

00:20:58.180 --> 00:20:59.190
Hey, Sis.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:02.900
You know I want to practice
my pitching too, right?

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:05.290
Just give me a little longer.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:07.720
I've got a tournament game
the day after tomorrow.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:10.020
Oh, fine.

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:13.830
Maybe I'll be a really nice 
big sister and pitch to you.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.160
You mean it?!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.170
Come on, Sis, let's go!

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.130
All right, all right.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:19.790
Let's go!

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.100
Dinner's almost ready.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:28.220
Honestly... There are baseball nerds
everywhere you look in this house.

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:26.890
Hey! Don't start with a curve ball!

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.880
Good work, everyone!

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:35.890
I'm gonna announce tomorrow's lineup
and hand out your numbers while I'm at it.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:38.710
Batting first, center field, Fujii Chisato.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:40.610
What? I'm leading off?

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:42.560
Chisato. You go, girl.

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:44.970
Batting second, shortstop, Sagara Tao.

00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:46.080
Right.

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:48.820
Dang, lost my spot as shock trooper captain.

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:51.620
Batting third, second base, Sawa Yayoi.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.790
Oh, okay, then.

00:21:53.130 --> 00:21:55.830
Batting fourth, catcher, Kawashima Anita.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:56.750
Okay!

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:59.610
Batting fifth, pitcher, Sakura Mutsuko.

00:21:59.610 --> 00:22:00.960
In the meat of the order?

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:04.160
Batting sixth, third base, Kandori Seira.

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:05.420
I'm number six?

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:07.950
Batting seventh, right field, Nishina Akira.

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:10.120
I-I'm way down the order?

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:12.480
Batting eighth, first base, Tanba Hiromu.

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:13.100
Got it!

00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:15.540
And lastly, batting ninth, left field.

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:16.570
That'll be me.

00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:18.060
Let's give it our best tomorrow!

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.730
Yeah!

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:20.910
All right!

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:27.740
<i>This will be the true beginning
of the new generation</i>

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:29.680
<i>of the Fuurin Middle baseball team.</i>

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:04.730
Looks like Daigo-kun's Fuurin team
is finally getting started, Goro-kun.

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:09.510
Yeah, and I'm so excited, I wanna
leap onto the field and go wild.

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:10.800
Wanna join me, Toshi?

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:11.900
That's just like you.

00:24:11.900 --> 00:24:13.800
But how's Daigo-kun handling it?

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.720
Whatever obstacle he faces,
he'll overcome it.

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:20.020
He's already gone through 
so much to get here.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Captain Daigo</b>

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:22.350
Next time: "Captain Daigo."

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:24.480
Run to the stage of your dreams!
